                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/552: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hornibrook</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-06T20:00:00-06:00">September 6, 1937—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 7—12:04 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>59. Following week-end surge of public sentiment favorable to such action and
                    apparently after consultation with Salvador, Costa Rican Government late this
                    afternoon offered mediation to Nicaragua and Honduras.</p>
                <p>Reports from Managua indicate that conflict was in process of adjustment before
                    this step taken.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hornibrook</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
